4 & 28.0 & 960   & +3329\% & 198  & 1.13$\times$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\paragraph{ROC analysis and threshold calibration.} We pool 120 datapoints from the 1.5B WikiText-2 and PubMed experiments and construct ROC curves for binary collapse detection (positive class: $\geq$75\% contamination). Table~\ref{tab:roc} reports AUC by signal and training progress checkpoint. Stable rank achieves AUC=0.97 at 5\% progress and 0.94 even at 3\%. By 10\% progress, both stable rank and perplexity reach AUC$\geq$0.97.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{Collapse detection AUC by signal and training progress. Binary label: $\geq$75\% contamination = collapsing. $n=120$ datapoints.}
\label{tab:roc}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
\toprule
Signal & 3\% & 5\% & 10\% & 20\% & 50\% \\
\midrule
Stable Rank    & 0.94 & 0.97 & 0.99 & 1.00 & 1.00 \\
Perplexity     & 0.88 & 0.93 & 0.97 & 0.99 & 1.00 \\
Token Entropy  & 0.86 & 0.91 & 0.95 & 0.98 & 1.00 \\
