\paragraph{Practical implication.} If a training corpus contains $\leq$50\% synthetic data, model collapse is self-limiting and monitoring suffices. Above ${\sim}$60\% contamination, active intervention---data filtering, mixing ratio adjustment---is necessary to prevent catastrophic collapse.


